@8738. The so-called saints, in Jupiter, wear a turreted hat of a dark colour. @SE 588.

@LJ 54. The beginning of Babylonish dominion is described by "the city and the tower whose head was in heaven."

@56[7]. The Babylonians have watch-towers built in the midst of their congregation, from which they can extend their sight into all the neighbouring parts.

@58[end]. Some were seen who were building a tower which reached up into Heaven where the Angels are; but this was only a representative of their machinations.

@TCR 69[2]. Like one who stands on a lofty tower. @SE 4393. @4506.

@121. Such an onslaught of the Hells is meant by "the tower built in the land of Shinar"... @276.

@SE 3734. (Quakerism) represented by a high, pointed, tower, of a grey colour...

@4965. See <Last Judgment>, @4966. @4979.

@4979[end]. For a tower = doctrine.

@DMin 4601. An immense tower seen.

@AE 315[15]. "Towers" (Isaiah 30:25) = doctrines of falsity. ( = those who are in evils and the derivati ve falsities; in special, those who are in the love of dominating by means of the holy things of the Church. @401[10].) ( = the falsities of doctrine which are from the love of self and of the world... for, in the Spiritual World, those who seek to rule by the things of the Church, build towers for themselves in high places. @405[6].)

@410[3]. "Tower," and "wall" (Isaiah 2:15) = confirmed falsities of doctrine. @514[9].

@453[10]. To "number her towers" (Psalms 48:12) = to consider the higher or interior truths of that Church.

@--[11]. "Towers" (Isaiah 33:18) = interior truths.

@654[53]. "From the tower of Seventh to the border of Cush" (Ezekiel 29:10) = from primes to ultimates.

@918[4]. "He built a tower in the midst of it" (Psalms 5:2) = the interior things into which there is influx, and through which there is communication with Heaven.

@922[7]. "And built a tower" (Matthew 21:33) = The interior truths from that good, which looked to Heaven.

