@9156. "Upon every word of transgression" (Exodus 22:9) = whatever injury and whatever loss; for "transgression" = everything that is contrary to the truth of faith, thus that which injures and extinguishes it, consequently whatever injury or loss there is of it.

@--. In the Word, evils are now called "sins," now "iniquities," and now "transgressions"... Those are called "transgressions" which take place contrary to the truths of faith... These, and "iniquities" issue from a perverted understanding. Illustrated.

@--[3]. As "transgressions" are things which are contrary to the truths of faith, they are also "transgressions -transgressiones-," and "revolts -defectiones-." Illustrated.

@--. That "transgression" = evil contrary to the truths of faith, is manifestly evident from these words.

@9309. "He will not bear your transgression" (Exodus 23:21) = because these things oppose truths from good; for "transgression" = the things which are contrary to the truths of faith; thus which are opposed to truths from good, which are the truths of faith.

