@10406[7]. "Treasures" (Jeremiah 50:37) = the Knowledges of truth and good. ( = the falsities of their doctrine. @AR 52[2].) ( = all things of doctrine. @AE 355[17].)

@TCR 759. The treasures accumulated by the Babylonians. Signified. @784.

@CL 527[2]. Like those who gather jewels into their treasuries...

@SE 2500[end]. Made friends of cooks and treasurers.

@4428. They have the phantasy that they see immense treasures of gold...

@5294. See <Last Judgment>. @5320. @5415. @5418.

@AE 131[4]. "Treasures" = Knowledges. @576[5]. @654[41]. @--[73]. @700[17].

@193[4]. "Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth... but in Heaven" (Matthew 6:19, 20). "Treasures" = the Knowledges of truth and good. To "lay them up in Heaven" = in the spiritual man.

@236[4]. "Gold and silver in thy treasures" (Ezekiel 28:4, 5) = the Knowledges of good, and the Knowledges of truth.

@275[11]. "He giveth the deeps for storehouses" (Psalms 33:7) = sensuous scientifics, which are the most general and ultimate things of the natural man, and in which are at the same time more interior truths. Hence they are called "storehouses."

@419[13]. Reformation through the Divine truth from Him is signified by, "He bringeth forth the wind out of His treasuries" (Psalms 135:7). ( = spiritual things in the Word from Heaven. @644[19].)

@622[3]. "Fill their belly with Thy treasure" (Psalms 17:14) = with the truth of the Word.

@714[17]. Spiritual treasures, which are the Knowledges of truth and good from the Word. Signified.

@840[10]. "The treasure hid in a field" (Matthew 13:44) = the Divine truth which is in the Word [as contained] in the Church. @863.

Treasures.; Gaza.
Treasury.; Gazophylarium.

