Tremble. Shake.; Tremiscere. Contremiscere. Intremiscere.
Tremor. Trembling.; Tremor.
Tremulously.; Tremiscenter.

@AC 3219. Some spirits fell on me... striking a tremor in my nerves and bones... @SE 2550.

@5502. "They trembled -intremuerunt- a man to his brother" (Genesis 42:28) = general terror. Explained.

@8312. "They trembled -contremuerunt-" (Exodus 15:14) = terror.

@8816. Under <Alarm>, see this reference.

@--[2]. They who are in good do indeed tremble -contremiscunt- at the presence of the Divine; but it is the holy tremor which precedes reception...

@8822. "The whole mountain trembled-tremiscebat exceedingly" (Exodus 19:18) = the commotion of Heaven.

@8917. A tremor such as there is when Divine truths are being received. Signified.

@AR 56. A holy fear which is sometimes conjoined with a holy tremor of the interiors of the mind... supervenes, when life from the Lord enters...

@SE 1934. Evil Spirits possessed the joints of my whole body with a tremor...

@3206. Sirens moved my hair and scalp tremulously.

@3586. Some of those who supposed they could do all things... began to tremble -tremulare- grossly... At the presence of a little one they staggered and trembled.

@3767. The influx of the (Spirits who actuate the Quakers) formerly threw them manifestly into a tremor... (It is not so great now. @LJPost 59.)

@4094. A certain celebrated Roman... then began to be moved with a kind of holy tremor...

@4806[end]. For a trembling seized all the bodies (of the Moravian Spirits), which terrified them.

@AE 282[6]. "Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me" (Psalms 55:5) = the distress (felt in temptation).

@304[15]. The Church is said to "shake and tremble -contremuisse-" (Psalms 18:6, 7) when it is perverted by the falsification of truths. @400[8].

@355[31]. The Church devastated is signified by "the whole land trembled -contremuit-" (Jeremiah 8:16).

@400[7]. When, in place of love to the Lord, there reigns the love of self... the mountains are said to "tremble contremiscere" (Nahum 1:5). @405[45].

@406[2]. That all the Knowledges... are then disturbed is signified by "the islands shall tremble -contremiscent-..." (Ezekiel 26:15).

@413[2]. They then experience such tremor... that they flee... @414, Signified.

@594[13]. "The earth trembled -contremuit-" (Judges 5:4) = the state of the Church then wholly changed.

@601[6]. The vehement power of Divine truth and the consequent terror is described by "the heavens and the earth shall tremble -contremiscent-" (Joel 3:16).

@650[41]. "The fishes... the bird... the wild beast... and every creeping thing... and every man... shall tremble -contremiscent- before Me" (Ezekiel 38:20) = that all things of man, as to the things of the Church with him, will be changed.

@677[8]. That the holy tremor which seizes upon, agitates, and convulses the interiors of the head, when the Divine inflows, is called "fear," etc. Illustrated.

Tremulous, To be.; Micare.
Beating, A.; Micatio.

