@AR 490[end]. A Trinal or Triune God is not one God when the Trinal and Triune is in three Persons; but He in whom the Trinal and Triune is in one Person, He is the One God.

@TCR 135. They replied, We think of three Gods from our idea about the Triune God.

@163. The Triune God has thus been treated of.

@627. Faith, imputation, and the merit of Christ, in the present Church, may be called a Triune; for if one of the three were taken away, modern theology would become nothing.

